## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Naming Decision: "Orion Hub"**
> The current plan renames the Mobile's `Orion Connect` feature to **"Orion Hub"** across the UI — the sidebar, the screen header, and all copy. The underlying module folders stay at `connect/` to avoid churn. Confirm if "Orion Hub" is the final name, or if you have a different branding in mind.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **TV Port: 8925**
> The plan assigns `port 8925` to TV's WebSocket server (Desktop is `8924`). This allows both Desktop and TV to run on the same LAN without collision, and the Mobile's discovery service can distinguish them by port + service type. Confirm this is acceptable.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Samsung Tizen Development Prerequisites**
> To deploy to your Samsung 7 Series TV, you'll need:
> 1. **Enable Developer Mode** on the TV (Apps → enter `12345` → set your PC's IP)
> 2. **Install Tizen Studio** (or use a lightweight CLI via `tizen-cli` / SDB)
> 3. **Create a Samsung developer certificate** (Author + Distributor certs tied to TV's DUID)
> 
> This is a one-time setup. The TV app is then pushed via WiFi using SDB. No Samsung Seller Office submission is needed for personal use.

> [!WARNING]
> **Samsung TV has NO physical remote for Orion**
> The TV app's UI is designed for **Mobile-only control**. There is no built-in D-pad navigation fallback. If the Mobile disconnects, the TV shows a "Connect Orion Hub" pairing screen. This is by design per your spec, but worth confirming — Samsung Seller Office certification (if ever desired) would require D-pad navigation support.

