## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Content sources on TV — what should TV play?**
> Desktop currently plays Cinema (streaming via embedded webviews/iframes), Local Video files, and Music. For TV:
> - **Cinema streams** — Yes, these will work via HTML5 video player on TV
> - **Local video** — Should TV support playing local files? (From USB? From network share? Or only Mobile-cast?)
> - **Music** — Should the TV app include the Music Planet experience, or is TV strictly video?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Cast from Mobile?**
> Should Mobile be able to "cast" content it's browsing directly to the TV? (e.g., user finds a movie on Mobile → taps "Play on TV" → TV starts playing). This is different from using Mobile purely as a remote for the TV's own browse UI.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Desktop ↔ TV interaction?**
> Should Desktop be able to cast/send content to TV, or is TV completely independent from Desktop (both controlled only via Mobile Hub)?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q4: TV Volume Control**
> When Mobile controls "volume" on TV, should it:
> - Control the **app-level** HTML5 video volume (software), OR
> - Control the **TV hardware volume** via Samsung Tizen API (`tizen.tvaudiocontrol`)?
> - Or both (a "TV Volume" and a "Media Volume" like we have system volume vs media volume on Desktop)?

