- **TV Screensaver** — ambient mode when idle

#### [NEW] `apps/tv/src/server/tvConnectServer.js`

**The TV's WebSocket server** — this is the TV equivalent of Desktop's [`smartConnectIpc.js`](file:///c:/Projects/Orion%20-%20A%20Multiverse%20of%20Stories/apps/desktop/src/main/ipc/smartConnectIpc.js):

- Runs an **HTTPS + WSS** server on port `8925` inside the TV app
- Handles pairing (PIN displayed on TV screen, entered on Mobile)
- Authenticates secure socket connections from Mobile
- Dispatches commands to the TV renderer (navigate, play, seek, volume, etc.)
- Broadcasts playback telemetry back to Mobile
- Reuses: `secureIdentity`, `secureTrust`, `pairingStore`, `controllerOwnership`, `reliableCommandScheduler` — all ported/imported from shared

> [!NOTE]
> Samsung Tizen web apps run in a WebKit-based browser environment. They support WebSocket, WebCrypto, and HTTPS via `fetch`. The server-side WebSocket will run via a **lightweight embedded WS server** within the Tizen app's service worker / background page, or via a Tizen Hybrid app with a native service component.

